From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Velez Garcia <velezgarciaemmanuel25@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 08:48:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Turn chunk retention on by default, and bound it

unloadDelayTicks was added in an earlier patch and defaulted to 0, so the
feature that stops a prison server reloading the same mine off the disk
every time a player walks out of it was shipped switched off.

It now defaults to 400 ticks (20 seconds), and gains a companion limit:
over unloadDelayChunkLimit loaded chunks the delay is dropped for that
pass, so a world under pressure unloads exactly as it would have without
retention and memory can never run away because of it.

Whether the delay is worth its memory is now answerable rather than a
guess - /vs perf chunks reports retains next to unloads, and the share of
chunk queue entries that never reached the disk.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/com/voidsoul/spigot/config/VoidSoulWorldConfig.java b/src/main/java/com/voidsoul/spigot/config/VoidSoulWorldConfig.java
index 9af7348910d00c5028d102c99f1ee09e310bfded..5f72825d592181c344a098ab811c36756f99362d 100644
--- a/src/main/java/com/voidsoul/spigot/config/VoidSoulWorldConfig.java
+++ b/src/main/java/com/voidsoul/spigot/config/VoidSoulWorldConfig.java
@@ -80,8 +80,24 @@ public class VoidSoulWorldConfig {
                 "the delay is simply taken out of the queue, with no disk I/O at all.\n" +
                 "0 keeps the vanilla behaviour of unloading as soon as possible.\n" +
                 "Reasonable values are 200-600 (10-30 seconds); higher values keep more\n" +
-                "chunks in memory.")
-        public int unloadDelayTicks = 0;
+                "chunks in memory.\n" +
+                "\n" +
+                "The cost is not only memory. A chunk waiting out its delay has not had\n" +
+                "removeEntities() called on it yet, so its entities are still in the world\n" +
+                "and still tick, subject to the activation range. Watch \"retained\" in\n" +
+                "/vs perf chunks: if it is not a large share of the unloads, the delay is\n" +
+                "only costing you.")
+        public int unloadDelayTicks = 400;
+
+        @Comment("Ignore unloadDelayTicks once a world has more than this many chunks\n" +
+                "loaded, so retention can never be the reason a server runs out of memory.\n" +
+                "\n" +
+                "Over the limit, chunks unload as soon as they are queued, exactly as they\n" +
+                "would with the delay off; under it, the delay applies again. A view distance\n" +
+                "of 10 keeps roughly 441 chunks per player in view, so a limit wants to be\n" +
+                "comfortably above what your player count actually needs.\n" +
+                "0 means no limit.")
+        public int unloadDelayChunkLimit = 0;
 
         @Comment("Maximum number of sky light columns re-checked per chunk per tick.\n" +
                 "\n" +
diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/ChunkProviderServer.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/ChunkProviderServer.java
index b8c66cc68b946786ddbd83296684df6c0967b826..c1906da3f78be9104d7993bca0c6d7eff61f5976 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/ChunkProviderServer.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/ChunkProviderServer.java
@@ -407,7 +407,17 @@ public class ChunkProviderServer implements IChunkProvider {
             int maxUnloads = this.world.voidsoulConfig.chunks.maxUnloadsPerTick;
             if (maxUnloads <= 0) maxUnloads = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
 
-            final int unloadDelay = this.world.voidsoulConfig.chunks.unloadDelayTicks;
+            int unloadDelay = this.world.voidsoulConfig.chunks.unloadDelayTicks;
+
+            // VoidSoulSpigot start - keep retention from being the reason we run out of
+            // memory: over the configured chunk limit the delay is simply dropped, so this
+            // world unloads exactly as it would have without it.
+            final int unloadDelayChunkLimit = this.world.voidsoulConfig.chunks.unloadDelayChunkLimit;
+
+            if (unloadDelayChunkLimit > 0 && this.chunks.size() > unloadDelayChunkLimit) {
+                unloadDelay = 0;
+            }
+            // VoidSoulSpigot end
             // Chunks whose delay hasn't elapsed yet. They are put back once the loop is
             // done, so they can't be popped again during this same pass.
             final java.util.List<Long> deferred = unloadDelay > 0 ? new java.util.ArrayList<Long>() : null;
